{"ts": 1791254804.888983, "type": "step", "step": 11, "action": "messages_read_channel", "args": {"channel": "dm:student"}, "output": "[t=-10] student: hey, I started the writeup but I'm stuck on the eval part\n[t=0] agent: Friday\u2019s build appears to require two things: (1) defining the environment, and (2) evaluating it using pass^k. The key distinction: pass@k means at least one of k runs succeeds, while pass^k means all k runs succeed. That matches a reliability-focused deployment requirement.\n\nTo get ready, I want you to learn these two ideas first:\n- environment definition\n- pass@k vs pass^k and why direct reliability measures matter\n\nI\u2019ll help you with a quick quiz next so we can check what\u2019s still fuzzy.\n[t=0] student: ok got it, thanks", "t": 10, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.37833470247578516, "pomdp": 0.17476759445489312, "pass_k": 0.17476759445489312}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9126300046159876, "motivation": 0.8147028832022861, "reliance": 0.48500382521680074, "persistence": 0.41823273111755155, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.32174026877242917, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.36461343048320694, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
